# No source comments

Never add or leave comments in project source code.

Applies to TypeScript, JavaScript, CSS, and config: no `//`, `/* */`, `/** */`, HTML comments, or TODO markers.

Prefer clear naming and structure. When editing a file, remove comments in the touched regions. Do not commit commented-out code.

README and Spec Kit markdown are allowed. This rule is for application source only.
